    />

    <div class="narrative prose">
      <SectionHeading id="evidence" rule={false}>What is first-hand here, and what is not</SectionHeading>
      <p>
        The stays behind this site were <strong>August 2023</strong> and
        <strong>August 2024</strong>, the second of them six nights in El Raval.
        La Boqueria and the Mercat de Sant Antoni were visited and photographed.
        The photographs on this page are all from those stays.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything about how the city eats — the clock, the formats, the
        vocabulary, the markets — is either durable cultural practice or was
        checked against official sources on <strong>4 August 2026</strong> and is
        dated accordingly. Where a market's hours or an establishment's status
        matters, the official page is linked rather than transcribed, because
        those move faster than any article.
      </p>
      <p>
        And where the record of a meal is thin, the page says so. A photograph
        of a shopfront proves someone stood at the door; it does not prove what
        was ordered. That distinction is kept throughout, and the honest
        accounting sits in its own section at the end.
      </p>
    </div>

